  "body": "# Summary\r\n\r\nSupport extended work coordinate offsets in the Mach3 post processor (`assets/posts/mach3.cps`).\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Increase `workOffsetMax` from 6 to 254 in `assets/posts/mach3.cps`.\r\n- Implement `offsetWord(value)` helper to output standard `G54`..`G59` for offsets 1 to 6.\r\n- Output `G59 P<n>` for extended offsets 7 to 254.\r\n- Refuse offsets less than 1 or greater than 254 with an explicit error message.\r\n- Update `onParameter` and `onSection` to use the formatted work offset string in operation notes and initial WCS blocks.\r\n- Add unit tests in `crates/post/tests/mach3_post.rs` verifying standard offsets, extended offsets, and refusal behavior.\r\n- Record design decision in `docs/decisions/4149-mach3-extended-work-offsets.md`.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\n- Public Mach3 G-code and programming manual (machsupport.com).\r\n- No vendor materials consulted.\r\n\r\n## Pinning Tests\r\n\r\n- `crates/post/tests/mach3_post.rs::mach3_work_offsets_g54_through_g59_and_extended_g59_p`: Verifies offsets 1..6 emit G54..G59, offsets 7..254 emit G59 P<n>, and offset 256 is refused.\r\n\r\n## Not Exercised\r\n\r\n- Physical machining execution on a Mach3 CNC machine controller.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Mach3 post: support extended work offsets G59 P7..P254.\r\n\r\nFixes #4149\r\n\r\n",
